    {
      "id": "6a769f1add0f065e8694567925c700a9a02271ea",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1200654231,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Doesn't `g_utf8_validate()`, which appeared earlier, do exactly the same thing as `g_utf8_validate_len()` if its length parameter (which is signed) is not -1 (which means to the end of a null terminated string)?\n\nOne thing about `g_utf8_make_valid`, `g_utf8_validate_len()`, and the others  is that they consider any internal nulls to be invalid and replace them / return false. \n\nI am not sure that we always want to do that, although perhaps sometimes we do. It doesn't make a difference here, but for something like FT_STRINGZPAD blindly changing null padding to replacement characters would be wrong.\n\nOn the other hand it prevents accidentally truncating on an internal null through string functions, since we don't use counted strings everywhere.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2022-12-08T01:30:12.299Z",
          "updated_at": "2022-12-08T01:30:12.299Z",
